body:
Part of #146 (the sheet layout part; Arabic letter joining / bidi is separate text-shaping work, see #260).

## Root cause
`view.rightToLeft` (Page Layout › Sheet Options), the `Sheet::right_to_left` flag and the XLSX `<sheetView rightToLeft="1">` round trip already existed on main, but the grid ignored the flag: an RTL sheet still drew column A on the left, and there was no ribbon control for it.

## What changed
- **Grid mirroring** (`crates/ui-egui/src/grid.rs`): the grid still computes its layout in logical left-to-right coordinates (`Geo::x`, `cell_rect`, `col_at`…) and then mirrors it across the grid's vertical centre line on screen:
  - painted shapes are reflected after painting (`mirror_painted`/`mirror_shape`). Rects, lines, paths and circles are flipped. Text galleys and meshes (pictures in cells) are only moved, so glyphs and images keep their direction. Default alignment therefore comes out as text on the right and numbers on the left, overflow runs to the left, and filter buttons, data bars, CF icons and the fill handle sit on the mirrored side;
  - floating charts, pictures and shapes move as a whole (`chartview::paint_objects` now reports the shape range each object painted), so a chart keeps its axes;
  - pointer input is mirrored back (`Geo::mirror_pos`) before hit-testing, so clicks, drags, header selection/resize, fill, move, object drag and context menus hit the right cells. Popup positions are converted back to screen coordinates;
  - the in-cell editor, text box editor, validation list/input message and note popups are placed on the mirrored side (the cell editor grows to the left);
  - the vertical scrollbar moves to the left. A horizontal trackpad swipe moves the content the way the fingers go;
  - Left/Right arrows follow the screen (Left goes to the next column), in the grid and in the editor's Enter/Point modes. Tab is unchanged.
- **Ribbon**: Page Layout › Sheet Options › **Sheet Right-to-Left** button (outlined when on), with a new icon…

Depends on the XLSX `_xlpm.` PR (#423, "XLSX: strip _xlpm. from LET/LAMBDA parameters on read, …"). This branch is stacked on it. Without that change the default fuzz run fails on seed 3: a `LET(x,…)` formula comes back from an XLSX save as `LET(_xlpm.x,…)`. Merge that PR first, or review only the top commit here.

## What changed
`tests::every_command_survives_empty_params` runs each command once, on its own. It can't find bugs that only show up after a sequence of commands (insert rows under a spill, undo, sort, paste into a table). This PR adds a sequence fuzzer for those, and fixes the bugs it found.

### Harness: `crates/engine/tests/command_sequence_fuzz.rs`
- Each seed picks a sample workbook (sales, budget, grades) and runs a reproducible random sequence of commands. Most come from a curated list of state-changing commands with hand-shaped params. The rest are drawn from every registered command, with params generated from its `params` doc string. A short `EXCLUDED` list skips commands that open or write files or render PDFs, with the reason for each.
- Invariants, checked during the run:
  - no command panics (a panic caught by `Session::execute` counts as a failure), and save, reload and recalculation don't panic either;
  - a non-undoable command doesn't change cell content;
  - the structure stays valid: active sheet in range, sheet and table names valid and unique, merges and tables on the sheet and not overlapping, legacy arrays anchored at their top-left cell, selection on the sheet;
  - a full recalculation from scratch gives the same values as the incremental recalculation;
  - every 10 steps and at the end of each episode, an XLSX save and reload gives the same sheets, formulas and values;
  - at the end of an episode (before the 100-step undo limit), undoing everything restores the starting workbook and redoing everything restores the final one (view state aside). The Watch Window list survives both.
- Environment variables: `GRIDCRAFT_FUZZ_SEEDS`…
